-->

## Directory Indexes

Each directory has an `index.cld` describing its contents.
Format and rules: `spec/dir-index-format.txt`.

- When looking for a file, check `index.cld` in the relevant directory
  first -- or run the `index-find` skill, which searches every index at
  once.
- When working in a directory that has no `index.cld`, create one
  before finishing.
- Keep `index.cld` current: update it in the same commit when you add,
  remove, or rename a file in that directory, or change what one does.

## Symbol Indexes

A source file may have a symbol index beside it, `<file>.cld` (for
`lib/util.js`, `lib/util.js.cld`), listing its symbols and, as `I`
entries, what it depends on. Format and rules:
`spec/file-index-format.txt`.

- When looking for a definition, use `symbol-find-<lang>` (js, py, sh,
  bash) before grepping source. Before naming a new symbol, use
  `symbol-dupecheck-<lang>`.
- Before changing what a file exports, use `symbol-deps rdeps <file>`
  to see what depends on it.
- Keep `<file>.cld` current in the same commit: add, remove or rename
  its entries with the symbols and dependencies, and rename or remove
  the index with its source.

## The Gate

`scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit` runs both checkers over the staged
commit -- renames and deletions included -- and blocks a commit whose
indexes have gone stale. Install it once per clone with
`./scripts/git-hooks/install.sh`. Run `index-audit-partial` before
committing to see a block coming.

There is no sanctioned bypass. The rule is fix the index.
